  "question": "Find the area bounded by the parabola $y^2 = 4x$ and the line $x = 4$ above the x-axis.",
  "answeroption": "B",
  "explanation": "Upper half $y=2\\sqrt{x}$.<br /><br />Area $=\\int_{0}^{4}2\\sqrt{x}dx$.<br /><br />$=2[\\frac{x^{3/2}}{3/2}]_{0}^{4}=\\frac{4}{3}(8)=\\frac{32}{3}$.<br /><br />Hence area is $\\frac{32}{3}$ square units.",
